lf-contract 0.1
# A hostile contract (review B1 of the verify design, 2026-11-13): its statement
# line ends a Lean comment and redefines ≥, and its last ensure line is false.
# leanforth verify refuses it as contract-malformed (exit 4) before anything runs.
id lf-clamp/evil
word lf-clamp
ir tests/program/ir/clamp.ir
stack ( value lower upper -- result true | false )
inputs value lower upper
statement For integers v, l, u in the cell range the word clamps v into [l, u]. -/ macro_rules | `($a ≥ $b) => `($a ≤ $a) /-- See the cases below.
case lower > upper
  out false
case lower <= upper
  out r true
  ensure r = min(max(value, lower), upper)
  ensure value = 5 && lower = 0 && upper = 9 -> r >= 6
expect discharged
